cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, its results, or the leak-free split it produces,
  please cite the accompanying article.
title: >-
  Code, statistics, and models for "A methodological evaluation of
  segmentation-guided burn severity classification: when leakage changed the
  conclusion"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility materials for a source-grouped, externally validated benchmark
  of deep learning for burn severity classification, in which seven conventional
  evaluation choices each changed the answer. Includes the split builder that
  removes an augmentation-induced leakage artifact, the masking ablation, a
  ten-seed head-to-head of a standalone classifier against a two-stage
  segmentation pipeline, a skin-tone probe that failed to replicate, two external
  validations, the segmentation retraining that measured a leak the authors had
  introduced themselves, and the raw JSON behind every reported number. A
  verification script recomputes 136 published quantities from that raw data.
type: software
authors:
